From 6051e4c8fe40202559e873254bf66ef0e7f2e72c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Bons <2526796+wingedsheep@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:47:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [agent-loop: claude-opus-5-5] Encore keyword for Commander
 staples (#3829)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* Add encore (CR 702.141) and player-directed attack requirements

MarkMustAttackEffect gains a `defender` axis — "attacks that opponent this turn
if able" — stored as MustAttackPlayerThisTurnComponent and enforced through
DirectedAttackRequirements beside Public Enemy (bound only while the creature
could attack that player, CR 508.1d). Encore composes from it: per opponent, a
token copy under the activator's control that gains haste, is marked to attack
that opponent, and is sacrificed at the next end step.

Impulsive Pilferer (CMR #185) is the first card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* Clear attacks-this-turn marks when a creature leaves the battlefield; doc fixes

Review follow-ups: the directed and undirected must-attack-this-turn marks belong
to the object (CR 400.7); SDK reference badge wording and helper list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

